[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: In response to the author's change to implement Pretense state machine, fake synthesis, unit tests, real implementation tests, and hypothesis stateful fuzzing for SemverSolver, two verification defects remain in benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py. First, in SemverSolverStateMachine.get_releases (lines 480-488), the antecedent guard ctx.requires(lambda check: check(len(self.state.packages) > 0, ...)) violates the contract in low/semver_solver.pyi for PackageRepository.get_releases, which mandates raising PackageNotFoundError whenever a queried package name is not registered in the repository, causing fake dispatch during test_fake_get_releases_not_found to fail with NoMatchingTransitionError instead of raising PackageNotFoundError when called on an empty repository. Second, in SemverSolverStateMachine.resolve (lines 547-550), _ensure_resolve_postconditions (lines 562-563), and make_sut (lines 940-941), the postcondition check queries unregistered singletons via check.get(VersionEngine) and check.get(PackageRepository), raising KeyError during SemverSolverFuzzTest; make_sut must register or return the constituent service singletons (VersionEngine, PackageRepository, DependencySolver) or pass target to _ensure_resolve_postconditions so that postconditions can inspect the resolved outcome against the contract requirements in low/semver_solver.pyi.
