[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: In response to the author's change to implement SemVer 2.0.0 parsing, precedence comparison, range algebra, package repository, and backtracking dependency solver, static unreachable code remains in the module. Specifically, in range compilation, the empty token check following clause string splitting is unreachable because empty union clauses are already filtered prior to tokenization. Additionally, in dependency resolution conflict compilation, the fallback branch handling empty non-root conflicting package sets represents an unreachable condition under normal solver execution. The library module must restructure the code to eliminate this unreachable code or annotate impossible branches and caller assumptions with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: <reason>)'.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: In response to the author's change to fix get_releases requires guard to allow matching on empty repositories and raising PackageNotFoundError, pass target to _ensure_resolve_postconditions, and register constituent service singletons in make_sut, the pretense suite lacks test cases and transition assertions for several specification behaviors. Specifically, the suite lacks unit test cases and transition assertions covering: precedence comparison between differing non-numeric pre-release identifiers according to ASCII lexical ordering; parsing syntax error branches for hyphen ranges with bound prefix operators, hyphen ranges missing upper bounds, unexpected hyphen tokens, and operators without target versions; range satisfaction evaluating hyphen ranges with pre-release or wildcard bounds; range satisfaction evaluating wildcard expressions qualified by relational, tilde, and caret operators; negative satisfaction evaluations for equality, inequality, and strictly greater than comparators; and dependency solver conflict detection when transitive package dependencies conflict with existing version assignments.
