[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: In response to the author's change to fix pre-release scope propagation in hyphen range evaluation, coverage deficits persist across several specification areas. Specifically, the pretense suite lacks unit test cases and transition assertions covering: parsing and range satisfaction for hyphen ranges possessing wildcard lower bounds, minor wildcard upper bounds, or pre-release upper bounds; parsing and range satisfaction for wildcard expressions modified by relational, tilde, and caret prefix operators (including star wildcards and zero-major or zero-minor caret expansions); and dependency solver resolution conflict detection when transitive package dependencies violate existing version assignments during resolution search. The pretense suite must incorporate test cases or transition assertions covering these specification requirements to achieve full statement coverage.
