[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: In response to the author's change to eliminate unreachable empty token check after clause splitting and redundant empty non-root conflicting package set fallback in dependency conflict resolution, a contract violation remains in VersionEngine._compile_range (lines 304-372) and VersionEngine.satisfies (lines 381-420). According to the postconditions for VersionEngine.parse_range and VersionEngine.satisfies in low/semver_solver.pyi, range expressions must support basic comparators including '!=' applied to wildcards, evaluating to True when a version satisfies the range constraint and False otherwise. In VersionEngine._compile_range, wildcard handling implements branches for '=', '==', '>', '>=', '<', '<=', '^', and '~', but omits handling for matched_op == '!='; consequently, when a range constraint contains a wildcard qualified by '!=' (such as '!=*'), no atomic comparators are generated, leaving atomic_comps empty and causing VersionEngine.satisfies to vacously evaluate to True for any candidate version instead of evaluating to False as required because no semantic version can satisfy an inequality constraint against a universal wildcard.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: Support != comparator for universal and partial wildcards in _compile_range and satisfies, evaluating != * to False for all versions
